    {
      "fileName": "challenge-insight.json",
      "id": "bvyCaOChX3lwKUn8",
      "name": "Challenge Insight",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "bvyCaOChX3lwKUn8",
        "folder": "3oq6iE8irLjlLcEE",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Challenge Insight",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "reaction"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature you can see Casts a Spell that is from the divine or occult tradition.</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The triggering caster must be able to hear and understand you.</p><hr /><p>Your deep grasp of the mystical lets you know exactly what to say to make others doubt how well they understand the source of their own power.</p>\n<p>Attempt a counteract check against the triggering spell. Your counteract rank is half your level rounded up. You use your Occultism modifier as your counteract modifier if the triggering spell is from the occult tradition, or your Religion modifier if the triggering spell is from the divine tradition.</p>\n<p>If you successfully counteract the spell, the caster becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 1} until the end of their next turn.</p>"
          },
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "day"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Palatine Detective Dedication"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Lost Omens Divine Mysteries"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "archetype",
              "auditory"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 8,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "cursebreaker.json",
      "id": "f1gxSpqjYryc1yc4",
      "name": "Cursebreaker",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "f1gxSpqjYryc1yc4",
        "folder": "3oq6iE8irLjlLcEE",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Cursebreaker",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr /><p>Using various implements and esoteric methods, you can attempt to remove a curse from an unfortunate victim. It takes 10 minutes to perform these rites on a willing creature, who must remain within your reach the entire time.</p>\n<p>Attempt to counteract one curse afflicting the creature; your counteract rank is half your level rounded up, and you use either your @Check[occultism] or @Check[religion] modifier as your counteract modifier. If the afflicted creature or the individual who placed the curse on the afflicted creature is the target of your active investigation through Pursue a Lead, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to this counteract check.</p>\n<p>If the curse comes from a cursed item or other external source, a success indicates that the target creature can rid itself of the cursed item, but it doesn't remove the curse from the item.</p>"
          },
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "day"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 10
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Palatine Detective Dedication"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Lost Omens Divine Mysteries"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "archetype",
              "concentrate",
              "healing",
              "manipulate"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 10,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "esoteric-spellcasting.json",
      "id": "YtfmSKoUFjnqEH0T",
      "name": "Esoteric Spellcasting",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "YtfmSKoUFjnqEH0T",
        "folder": "3oq6iE8irLjlLcEE",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Esoteric Spellcasting",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Your study of a variety of esoteric texts and supernatural matters has broadened your mind and improved your spellcasting. Choose a 1st-rank occult or divine spell. You can cast this spell once per day as an innate spell. At 6th level, you gain a 2nd-rank spell of the same tradition you chose, and at 8th level, you gain a 3rd-rank spell, also of that tradition.</p><hr /><p><strong>Special</strong> You can take this feat a second time, choosing spells from the other available tradition.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
          "maxTakable": 2,
